Pixel Pet

About the Project
Pixel Pet is a small desktop companion that will display a cute pixel pet on an OLED screen. I wanted to make something fun that I could keep on my desk while also learning more about electronics and coding. This is my first time working on a project like this, so I am learning as I go. :) 

The Idea
The idea is to have a little character displayed on a screen that can sit on my desk. I want to make it simple but still fun to look at. Eventually, I hope to add different expressions or small animations to make the pet feel more alive.

Materials
The main parts of this project are an SSD1306 OLED display, a microcontroller, and a custom PCB. The OLED is the screen that will show the pet, and the microcontroller will run the code that controls what appears on it.

PCB Design
I am using KiCad to make the schematic and PCB layout. The schematic shows how the different parts connect, and the PCB layout is where I arrange the parts and connect them with traces.
I am still learning how to use KiCad, especially how to choose footprints and route the connections between the pads. I am working on making sure the connections match the schematic and that the board is laid out correctly.

Progress
Right now, I am working on the circuit design and PCB layout. I still need to finish connecting everything, maybe trying out extra code if im feeling up to it, and test the display with the controller. I will add more pictures and updates as I make progress.
